    "sourceOriginal": "C(α)=2^(t′−1) iff α ends in 10^j *^k (no star before 1).",
    "projectReplacement": "C(α)=2^(t′−1) iff α ends in *10^j *^k, j,k≥0.",
    "reasoning": [
      "The exercise uses literal stars for free bits and defines t′ as the count to the left of the last fixed bit. Appended free bits merely replace each reflected Gray prefix with one consecutive block, so stripping trailing stars preserves C and gives t=t′.",
      "By printed (a), C=2^t−2^(t−1)e_t−⋯−e_1, e_i is 1 iff the suffix after the i-th star matches the bitstring 1 then only zeros, of the same suffix length.",
      "For t>0 the final star has only fixed bits after it. Thus e_t=1 iff it is followed by 10^j; adding the stripped stars gives precisely the proposed ending. If e_t=1, for each earlier star the later fixed 1 lies after the first position of that star's suffix, so no earlier suffix matches 10…0 and all earlier e_i are 0.",
      "If e_t=0, all earlier possible subtractions total at most 2^(t−1)−1, so C≥2^(t−1)+1. If t′=0, C=1 and equality to 1/2 cannot hold, and the proposed pattern also cannot match. If there is no fixed bit, the sole entire-cube cluster has the same outcome under t′=0."
    ],
